<article class="env-lemma" id="00RK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00RK">Lemma <span data-tag="00RK">10.130.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $R \to S$ be of finite type. Let $R \to R'$ be any ring map. Set $S' = R' \otimes _ R S$. Denote $f : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S') \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S)$ the map associated to the ring map $S \to S'$. Set $W$ equal to the set of primes $\mathfrak q$ such that the fibre ring $S_{\mathfrak q} \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$, $\mathfrak p = R \cap \mathfrak q$ is Cohen-Macaulay, and let $W'$ denote the analogue for $S'/R'$. Then $W' = f^{-1}(W)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Trivial from Lemma <a href="/tag/00RJ" data-tag="00RJ">10.130.6</a> and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>